   "evidence": "`Unimodular.lean:172-173`: `def steinberg : d.AmbientGroup \u2192* d.AmbientGroup := d.1.1.geckFrobenius`, so the family-level form is still `rfl`. `Unimodular.lean:178-180` states `steinberg_eq_geckFrobenius` is \"deliberately not a `simp` lemma: `steinberg_geckRootSubgroup` and `coe_steinberg_apply` are the normal forms ... unfolding to `TauCeti.ValidLieTypeIndex.geckFrobenius` would keep them from firing\" \u2014 the branch equations as written hand the consumer the form that family API is built to avoid.",
   "file": "TauCeti/GroupTheory/SpecificGroups/CFSG/Assembly/GraphTwisted.lean",
   "fix": "Use `UnimodularExceptionalIndex.steinberg \u27e8\u27e8\u27e8_, hv\u27e9, by simp\u27e9, h\u27e9` in the `E8 | F4 | G2` alternative and in the three branch equations \u2014 exactly as `frobenius_E6`/`frobenius_E7` name `TypeE6LieIndex.steinberg`/`TypeE7LieIndex.steinberg` \u2014 and close the three cases of `frobenius_simpleRootSubgroup` with `UnimodularExceptionalIndex.steinberg_geckRootSubgroup \u27e8\u27e8\u27e8_, hv\u27e9, by simp\u27e9, h\u27e9 (.inl i) u`, as `steinberg_simpleRootSubgroup` already does at l.536-541.",
   "issue": "On `E\u2088`, `F\u2084`, `G\u2082` the new `frobenius` is `ValidLieTypeIndex.geckFrobenius \u27e8_, hv\u27e9` (l.187-188), one level below the `UnimodularExceptionalIndex` API that `AmbientGroup` (l.127), `simpleRootSubgroup` (l.166) and `steinberg` (l.207) use on those same branches; `frobenius_E8` (l.383-386), `frobenius_F4` (l.402-405), `frobenius_G2` (l.421-424) and the three proof cases (l.493-498) inherit it. So `frobenius` and `steinberg`, which are literally the same map there, get branch equations in two different normal forms, and the definition's own docstring (l.175-176, \"on the nine untwisted families that is the family's Steinberg endomorphism itself\") is not what `frobenius_E8` delivers.",
   "line": "187"
  }
 ],
